# Example: src/payments/CLAUDE.md

This is an example of a subdirectory-level `CLAUDE.md`, shown here as `subdir-CLAUDE.md.example`
so it doesn't get picked up as a real config file in the scaffold itself. Copy it to the actual
subdirectory as `CLAUDE.md` and edit the contents.

It demonstrates the additive-loading pattern from the root `CLAUDE.md`: this file does NOT repeat
the repo map or global gotchas — Claude already has those from the root file by the time it reads
this one. It only adds what's local to this subsystem.

---

## Scope

Payment processing and reconciliation. Talks to the external billing provider via `billing_client.py`;
everything else in this directory assumes that client's retry/idempotency behavior.

## Local test/lint commands (override root)

- Test: `pytest src/payments --maxfail=1` (root's full suite is too slow for iterating here)
- Lint: same as root

## Local conventions / gotchas

- `Invoice.amount` is stored in cents as an int, not a Decimal — a past bug came from treating it as dollars.
- `reconcile_batch()` silently swallows `ProviderTimeoutError` and retries once; this is intentional (billing provider is flaky under load), not a bug to "fix" without checking with the DRI first.
- There is no test for the partial-refund path (`process_refund(partial=True)`). Coverage here is 0%, not the misleadingly-high number the root README claims for the repo overall — do not assume this path works without characterization-testing it first.

## Last updated

Proposed by `stop-propose-doc-updates.sh` on 2026-08-01, reviewed and merged by DRI on 2026-08-03.
This line exists to demonstrate the documentation feedback loop in action — real subdirectory files
should keep an honest record of when local notes were last verified against the code.
